        "exam_year": "2022",
        "question_text": "<p>If $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$ and $\\theta$ is acute, find $\\cos \\theta$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the Pythagorean identity: $\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$.<br>Substitute $\\sin \\theta = \\frac{3}{5}$: $\\left(\\frac{3}{5}\\right)^2 + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$.<br>$\\frac{9}{25} + \\cos^2 \\theta = 1$.<br>$\\cos^2 \\theta = 1 - \\frac{9}{25} = \\frac{16}{25}$.<br>$\\cos \\theta = \\frac{4}{5}$ (since $\\theta$ is acute).</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
